	"provenance": "Provenance: Joseph Green Cogswell; Mortimer Leo Schiff; Moore S. Achenbach;\r\nCogswell no.294 , Hellman no.286 as   “Magdalen” by an unascribed Italian artist ,with note of relationship to AFGA's 1963.24.104 r-v and artist  “ of high rank” (George S. Hellman, Original Drawings by the Old Masters: The Collection formed by Joseph Green Cogswell, 1786-1871, New York: privately published, 1915);\r\nSuggested attributions; see beow;\r\nNote that  in 1977 Lynn Orr suggested circle of Bartolomeo Biscaino for this drawing and related 1963.24.104 (Regional Styles of Drawing in Italy: 1600-1700, 1977, cat. no. 37, p. 66);\r\nGiovanna Bertazzoni, 1.22.1997: I showed a photographic reproduction of the drawing to Professor Giulio Bora (Universita' di Milano), 10.17.1996, who disagrees with an attribution to an Italian artist --as well as for 1963.24.104. He suggests fo the two drawings a Northern European attribution;",
